# Intent: Train 3 item 14, mood that depends on care, saved across days (features.md Touch and play). A head pet adds care (4 points, at most 12 counted a day and one every 20 seconds); each whole day with no pet takes 12 away (at most 14 days counted); a new unit starts at 50. The resting face shows it: care 70 or more is happy, under 30 is sad, otherwise the plain face (3 point hysteresis so it never flickers). The record is 8 bytes (magic, version, care, pets today, day, checksum) in its own NVS namespace, written at most every 15 minutes and at a day change, so it lasts across days and reboots; a bad record is thrown away for the start state. A mood change pushes a `mood` event. Two tools: self.mood.get and self.mood.test (care 0 to 100 for now and not saved, -1 puts the saved value back). Rides the one-second daily tick and the existing head-touch event: no task, no timer, no heap.
